<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees Feb CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees Feb CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its February consumer price index stood at -0.2 percent month-on-month and 2.0 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In January, the Venice inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.7 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		  -0.2   (0.1)	2.0   (2.7)</p>
<p>    Food			     -0.5   (0.0)	0.4   (1.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.1   (0.0)	4.0   (3.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges-1.6   (0.5)	2.5   (4.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.1   (0.0)	1.9   (3.6)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.3   (2.6)	2.6   (2.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.0  (-0.8)	3.1   (3.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.1  (-0.1)     -1.9  (-1.6)</p>
<p>    Education			-3.5   (0.0)	2.3   (6.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.5   (0.0)	5.6   (6.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services     0.4   (0.4)	0.7   (0.9)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
